      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic secret management task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nThe initial file fetch_api_key.py is already implemented. Read it before generating the remaining files, and leave it unchanged.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_api_key.py - fetches an API key from a managed secrets store\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_db_secret.py - fetches a database connection secret at runtime\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] parse_json_secret.py - retrieves and parses a JSON-formatted secret\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] rotate_secret_version.py - reads a specific secret version or staged value\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] security_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Secret Management\n6. [HELPER] security_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Secret Management\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] rotation_summary.py - Summarize secret rotation status\n8. [LATER-STEP] secret_label_safety.py - Check secret labels and notes for unsafe text\n9. [LATER-STEP] secret_audit_embedding.py - Embed secret audit notes for semantic search\n10. [LATER-STEP] runbook_translate.py - Translate secret-rotation runbook notes\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
